WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.698
Host: Describe the portal triad while
distinguishing the figure's main relationship
from its simplification.

2
00:00:06.698 --> 00:00:13.062
Guide: The portal vein is posterior; the bile
duct and proper hepatic artery are anterior.

3
00:00:13.062 --> 00:00:17.955
Guide: Conventionally the duct is right and
artery left from the patient's perspective.

4
00:00:17.955 --> 00:00:23.794
Guide: The figure is a front–back relationship
schematic rather than a complete operative
view.

5
00:00:23.794 --> 00:00:27.832
Host: In a conventional anterior view of the
portal triad,

6
00:00:27.832 --> 00:00:32.156
Host: where is the bile duct relative to the
proper hepatic artery?

7
00:00:32.156 --> 00:00:38.509
Guide: On the patient's right. The duct
conventionally lies to the patient's right of
the proper

8
00:00:38.509 --> 00:00:41.983
Guide: hepatic artery; variants exist.
